r"""apply_handover_v33.py -- record that no regeneration is planned and hand the warmstart to
Phase 0 / M5 (docs only).

    python apply_handover_v33.py --root . --dry-run
    python apply_handover_v33.py --root .
    python verify_handover_v33.py --root .

Decided 2026-10-11:
  * the three defaults of v32 stand, without ablations (recorded as untested alternatives);
  * DATASET_V3_SPEC §0 #17 (SP-BP tie order), #18 (held-out seed coupling) and #19 (anchors)
    are accepted for data\v3m with usage rules -- none needs a regeneration;
  * §12 item 16: what M5 inherits (fresh-seed baseline for the warmstart, one M5 seed from
    student_2000, exploration designed in, no deduplication of RL transitions, SP-BP
    baselines with node-id tie order, generalisation on evaluation seeds only, ...).
No code changes; no code-signature module is touched.

DOCS
  docs/DATASET_V3_SPEC.md        status; §0 #17-#19 accepted with rules; §12 items 9-11;
                                 items 16 (handover) and 17 (untested alternatives).
  docs/CLAUDE.md                 where to read project state (the report is a dated record);
                                 results/m5_masked is not the warmstart source; status.

Assertion-guarded str.replace, as docs/CLAUDE.md requires: every anchor must match exactly
once, all edits are staged in memory, nothing is written unless every anchor in every file
matches. A file whose guard string is present is skipped (idempotent). Reads with universal
newlines, writes LF.
"""
